MonoBehaviour:
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 075ae7a4e0c44354e9959697c9e269fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: Buy Their Loyalty Legacy
  legacyName: Court Politics
  description: 'Governors gain +5 Opinion of the government.'
  flavorText: 'The failed coup taught the government that loyalty was rarely produced by ideology alone. Offices, access, prestige, concessions, personal rivalries, and the simple desire to be heard could determine whether a powerful figure defended the regime, ignored its danger, or joined those plotting against it. Rulers became more attentive to the political ecosystem surrounding formal authority, learning when a grievance could be settled cheaply before it became expensive to suppress. Critics called the resulting system patronage; its practitioners preferred realism. A court survived not merely by knowing who possessed power, but by knowing what each powerful person wanted.'
  policyPointCost: 1
  attackBonus: 0
  defenseBonus: 0
  movementBonus: 0
